# Swift UI file standards (`Calmscient/Swift UI/`)

When adding or editing any Swift file under `Calmscient/Swift UI/` (views, view models, models, hosting controllers):

## File header

After the filename / project lines, include author and date:

```
//
//  <FileName>.swift
//  Calmscient
//
//  <optional one-line purpose>
//
//  Vivek
//  15 May 2026
//
```

Use the **current date** when creating the file; do not omit this block.

## SwiftUI `View` previews

For every `struct …: View`:

1. **Always** add at least one `#Preview` at the bottom of the same file (after the main type).
2. Wrap previews in `#if DEBUG`.
3. Match the view’s `@available` (e.g. iOS 16) on preview helpers and `#Preview` when required.
4. Use a realistic `ViewModel` or a small `fileprivate` preview host (e.g. `@FocusState`, `@State` bindings) when the view needs bindings.
5. Use descriptive preview names (`#Preview("…")`) when multiple previews exist.

Do not leave new SwiftUI views without a working preview unless technically impossible (rare).

## UIKit hosting controllers

For `*HostingController` types that embed SwiftUI, add a preview in `Calmscient/Swift UI/general/SwiftUIHostingControllerPreviews.swift` using `UIViewControllerRepresentable` + `#Preview`, unless the hosting file already owns a dedicated preview.
